chapter('Build your first app shell', 'Replace the counter with a small hotel welcome screen.',
    '<p>A widget describes part of the screen. <code>build</code> returns that description. MaterialApp supplies navigation and theme. Scaffold gives a page an app bar and body. SafeArea avoids system cutouts. StatelessWidget has no changing internal state. Hot reload updates most code while the app runs; a full restart is needed after changing startup configuration.</p>',
    '<p>Delete the generated <code>test/widget_test.dart</code>, which refers to the old counter. Replace <code>lib/main.dart</code> with this complete temporary shell.</p>'+code(mini,'lib/main.dart — temporary complete replacement'),
    verify='fvm flutter run', checkpoint='You see LuxeStays and Find your next stay. Keep this main.dart until the course explicitly replaces it.')
chapter('Add a theme and reusable widgets', 'Build visual consistency before adding networking.',
    '<p>A theme shares colors and typography. Padding gives content space; Row lays children side by side; Column stacks them. Expanded takes remaining space. ListView scrolls. A reusable widget accepts inputs instead of reaching into unrelated app state. Text labels and semantic descriptions help screen readers.</p>',
    files=['lib/app/theme.dart','lib/shared/widgets/app_panel.dart','lib/shared/widgets/section_heading.dart','lib/shared/widgets/app_snack_bar.dart'],
    body='<p>After creating the files below, modify the temporary main.dart: add <code>import \'app/theme.dart\';</code> and change <code>const MaterialApp(home: Welcome())</code> to <code>MaterialApp(theme: AppTheme.light(), darkTheme: AppTheme.dark(), home: const Welcome())</code>. Removing the outer const is necessary because the theme is built at runtime.</p>', verify='fvm flutter analyze\nfvm flutter run', checkpoint='The welcome page uses the LuxeStays palette. Try light/dark mode and large system text.')
chapter('Represent failure and money', 'Introduce small shared types that can be tested without a screen.',
    '<p>Money stores minor units (cents for USD). A Failure carries a user-facing message and a diagnostic description. A sealed Result is either Ok(data) or Err(failure). Mapping transforms a successful result while preserving failure. These types stop raw network exceptions and floating-point prices spreading through widgets.</p>',
    files=['lib/core/error/failure.dart','lib/core/result.dart','lib/core/utils/money.dart','lib/core/utils/date_x.dart','lib/core/utils/ids.dart','lib/core/logging/app_logger.dart','lib/core/analytics/analytics.dart','lib/shared/widgets/app_states.dart'],
    verify='fvm dart analyze lib/core lib/shared',checkpoint='Shared code analyzes. The welcome UI remains usable while you build the foundations.', trouble='Create all files in this stage before analyzing: Result imports Failure, and analytics imports the logger. No network is involved yet.')
chapter('Model guests, rooms and reservations', 'Create immutable domain objects.',
    '<p>Domain means the hotel business concepts rather than screen or HTTP details. A stay contains arrival/departure; occupancy contains adults and child ages; an offer combines room, rate and dates. <code>copyWith</code> returns a changed copy, allowing state updates without mutating a value shared elsewhere.</p><p>Read the small search/media/hotel types first, then rate, loyalty, cart and booking. Notice how totals derive from nightly prices. Never rename a currency without converting its numeric value; this demo uses USD.</p>',
    files=['lib/domain/search.dart','lib/domain/media.dart','lib/domain/hotel.dart','lib/domain/rate.dart','lib/domain/loyalty.dart','lib/domain/cart.dart','lib/domain/booking.dart'],verify='fvm dart analyze lib/domain',checkpoint='The app can describe a booking independently of its UI or provider payloads.')
chapter('Configure requests and token storage', 'Build one consistent HTTP boundary.',
    '<p>Configuration supplies public URLs and identifiers through <code>--dart-define</code>. These are compiled into the binary and are not secret storage. A token is a temporary credential issued after authentication; store it in platform secure storage. PKCE is a proof used during OAuth login, explained when identity is connected.</p><p>An interceptor runs around an HTTP request: attach a correlation ID, add an issued token, log redacted diagnostics, or retry a transient failure. GET can be retried safely. A booking POST needs a server-supported replay guarantee; our demo idempotency key is not a claim about SynXis.</p>',
    files=['lib/core/config/app_config.dart','lib/core/storage/token_store.dart','lib/core/error/error_mapper.dart']+glob('lib/core/network/**/*.dart'),verify='fvm dart analyze lib/core',checkpoint='The request layer compiles with bounded timeouts and typed error mapping.',trouble='Use full URLs including http:// for local development. Never put provider secrets in dart-defines. The server will be introduced next; connection failures are expected until it runs.')
chapter('Create your local mock services', 'Run the server before wiring it to screens.',
    '<p>HTTP pairs a method and path with a request body, headers and status code. JSON is text containing objects, arrays and primitive values. Shelf turns a Dart function into a request handler. The Router matches paths. Fixtures are fictional data. Begin with support/fixtures/png, then each route file, web pages, and server.dart last.</p><p>Each file below is a separate lesson. Read one route at a time: input → validation → state change → response. A process restart resets reservations, quotes, points and payments. The mock is suitable for trusted local development only.</p>',
    files=['tool/mock_server/support.dart','tool/mock_server/fixtures.dart','tool/mock_server/png.dart','tool/mock_server/web_pages.dart','tool/mock_server/payment_routes.dart','tool/mock_server/synxis_routes.dart','tool/mock_server/property_hub_routes.dart','tool/mock_server/cms_routes.dart','tool/mock_server/salesforce_routes.dart','tool/mock_server/leonardo_routes.dart','tool/mock_server/server.dart'],
    verify='fvm dart run tool/mock_server/server.dart\n# In a SECOND terminal:\ncurl http://localhost:8080/health',checkpoint='Health returns status ok and a hotel count. Leave this terminal running.',trouble='Address already in use means another process owns port 8080. Stop your previous server or choose --port 8081 and use that port in every URL. Do not run two commands sequentially in the server terminal: the server intentionally keeps running.')
chapter('Decode and verify the booking gateway', 'Connect domain offers to the demo JSON contract.',
    '<p>A DTO (data-transfer object) mirrors one response format. Its fromJson constructor checks fields. A mapper converts that DTO into domain data. SynxisApi is retained as the adapter name, but its shopping/create/cancel shapes are local BFF assumptions. Property Hub retrieval uses separate lower-camelCase fields and integer IDs.</p><p>The quote store keeps the original nightly prices and promotion; re-quote compares totals before payment. Idempotency means a repeated operation has one effect. The reservation route rejects a reused key with a changed body.</p>',
    files=glob('lib/integrations/synxis/*.dart'),verify='fvm dart analyze lib/integrations/synxis',checkpoint='The booking client and mappers compile. No live SynXis credentials are required.',trouble='Do not substitute a SynXis production URL. Read the API audit in the final chapter before adapting any real provider.')
chapter('Enrich content and images', 'Add editorial content and licensed-media abstractions.',
    '<p>Contentful entries have fields and references; included assets resolve linked images. This app uses REST, not GraphQL. Leonardo Worldwide is hospitality media management. Leonardo.Ai is a different product; its optional legacy-shaped demo is not a current production integration.</p><p>A repository may cache data or tolerate missing editorial content. The hotel can still be bookable if its marketing headline is unavailable. A media provider returns an appropriate rendition for the displayed size; the mock serves gradients rather than external photography.</p>',
    files=glob('lib/integrations/cms/*.dart')+glob('lib/integrations/leonardo/*.dart'),verify='fvm dart analyze lib/integrations/cms lib/integrations/leonardo',checkpoint='Content and media adapters compile. Images in the mock work without internet access.')
chapter('Add identity, rewards and payments', 'Model member state and hosted payment intents.',
    '<p>OAuth authorizes access without giving the app a provider password. PKCE binds the authorization callback to the initiating client. The sample membership sign-in bypass is for mocks only. Loyalty points and voucher processes are fictional program rules; a real Salesforce org determines its fields, processes and API version.</p><p>A payment intent is a reference to a payment attempt. The hosted page returns a hint; the app verifies its status through the BFF. The demo collects no real card data and makes no PCI compliance claim.</p>',
    files=glob('lib/integrations/salesforce/*.dart')+glob('lib/integrations/payments/*.dart'),verify='fvm dart analyze lib/integrations',checkpoint='All integration clients compile and remain replaceable behind their repositories.')
chapter('Compose repositories and state', 'Connect dependencies and introduce Riverpod gradually.',
    '<p>Dependency injection means supplying collaborators rather than creating hidden global instances. A Provider constructs a service. <code>ref.watch</code> subscribes to changes; <code>ref.read</code> takes its current value; <code>ref.onDispose</code> closes resources. A Notifier stores state and exposes actions. An AsyncValue is loading, data or error.</p><p>The hotel repository combines inventory, content and media. BookingRepository coordinates re-quote, payment verification and booking. The search controller uses a request counter so a slow old response cannot overwrite a newer search. Build services first, then the composition root, then controllers.</p>',
    files=glob('lib/data/*.dart')+['lib/app/providers.dart','lib/features/account/session_controller.dart','lib/features/cart/cart_controller.dart','lib/features/search/search_controller.dart','lib/features/home/offers_provider.dart','lib/features/hotel/hotel_detail_controller.dart','lib/features/booking/checkout_controller.dart'],verify='fvm dart analyze lib',checkpoint='All services and controllers compile; the small welcome screen still runs.',trouble='Riverpod 3 removed older exported family type names. Keep inferred family provider declarations as shown. State mutation during build is avoided by the scheduled first search.')
