chapter('Show real mock-backed search results', 'Replace the welcome page with a working search.',
    '<p>ConsumerWidget can read provider state while building. The search page watches SearchState, shows a loading skeleton, then results or a retry message. Rebuilding is Flutter’s normal way to update the display; do not manually repaint widgets.</p>',
    code(preview,'lib/main.dart — complete search preview replacement')+'<p>At this checkpoint search, filters and adding a room work. Named navigation targets are added in the next stage; do not tap cart/detail links yet.</p>',files=['lib/features/search/search_screen.dart','Makefile'],
    verify='make run-emulator\n# iOS simulator instead: make run HOST=localhost',checkpoint='Search results load from the local server. Change dates to four nights and filter rooms.',trouble='Android emulator uses 10.0.2.2 for your computer. localhost means the phone itself unless adb reverse is configured. Changing dart-defines requires a full stop/restart, not hot reload.')
chapter('Build detail, cart and rewards pages', 'Give the search actions destinations.',
    '<p>A route is a page on a navigation stack. Arguments carry the hotel ID and name. Detail uses a family provider so each hotel loads independently. The cart stores selected offers, exposes totals and supports removal. Rewards show member balances and benefits. A page is composed from the same panels and states you already built.</p>',
    files=['lib/features/hotel/hotel_detail_screen.dart','lib/features/cart/cart_screen.dart','lib/features/loyalty/loyalty_screen.dart'],
    verify='fvm dart analyze lib',checkpoint='The three pages compile. Complete the WebView and checkout stages before switching to the full router.',trouble='These screen classes use route names already defined in the temporary router. The final route table comes after all destination classes exist.')
chapter('Connect safe hosted WebViews', 'Embed pages with a typed message bridge.',
    '<p>The JavaScript channel carries text; decode and validate it before using it. A bridge message names a type and payload. A stream emits successive bridge events. Deduplication prevents double handling. Navigation is limited to configured HTTP(S) origins and selected app deep links. A deep link uses a custom URL scheme, such as luxestays://payment-success.</p><p>A page-reported payment success is not proof of payment. The controller checks the expected intent and asks the server. A real provider may require system-browser authentication or additional trusted redirect origins. Never allow every URL to make a demo work.</p>',
    files=glob('lib/webview/bridge/*.dart')+['lib/webview/hybrid_webview.dart','lib/webview/payment_webview_screen.dart','lib/webview/booking_engine_webview_screen.dart','lib/webview/cms_content_webview_screen.dart'],verify='fvm dart analyze lib/webview',checkpoint='The native WebView integration compiles. It runs on Android/iOS; browser-only Flutter web is not a substitute for testing these pages.')
chapter('Finish checkout and navigation', 'Complete search → cart → hosted authorization → confirmation.',
    '<p>A Form groups validated inputs. Validation runs before creating payment. Await each transaction step in order. The controller rejects concurrent starts and mismatched completion hints. Total booking failure requests a demo authorization void; an uncertain void must be reported honestly.</p><p>Create checkout and confirmation first. Then replace the temporary router and main.dart with their final versions. AppRouter now imports every real destination. The final entry point installs error hooks and creates the provider container.</p>',
    files=['lib/features/booking/checkout_screen.dart','lib/features/booking/confirmation_screen.dart','lib/app/router.dart','lib/app/app.dart','lib/main.dart'],verify='fvm flutter analyze\nmake run-emulator',checkpoint='The complete native app can navigate from search to confirmation using synthetic guest/payment data.',trouble='If checkout reports changed prices, search again for a fresh offer. Restarting the server invalidates in-memory quotes. Never enter real card or guest information in this mock.')
chapter('Rehearse loading, failure and accessibility', 'Make the experience usable when services or layouts vary.',
    '<p>Loading is temporary, empty is a valid result, and failure offers recovery. Keep these distinct. Retry lets a guest recover after restoring the network. Errors should explain the action the guest can take without exposing raw payloads. An accessibility label explains an icon or image; a tooltip helps identify an action.</p><ol><li>Search an unavailable destination or an occupancy larger than every room; confirm an empty result.</li><li>Stop the server, search, then restart and retry.</li><li>Use 200% text scaling, a small phone, landscape and a screen reader. Scroll to all checkout fields and actions.</li><li>Check light/dark text contrast and clear field labels. Native WebView accessibility also needs a device pass.</li></ol>',
    code('fvm dart run tool/mock_server/server.dart --latency 25000\n# Or restart with intermittent faults:\nfvm dart run tool/mock_server/server.dart --fail-rate 0.15'),verify='fvm flutter analyze',checkpoint='You can explain and demonstrate loading, empty and error recovery states. This manual pass does not constitute a full accessibility certification.')
chapter('Add automated regression tests', 'Protect behavior instead of only checking compilation.',
    '<p>A unit test checks a small behavior, a widget test renders Flutter widgets in a test environment, and an integration test runs on a device. A test sets up inputs, performs an action and asserts the outcome. Overrides supply predictable dependencies. Mock contract tests validate our gateway behavior; they cannot detect a vendor change without updated official evidence.</p><p>Add core and model tests first, then controller/widget/bridge tests, then the booking lifecycle test. The four-night test protects the re-quote regression and verifies idempotency, authorization and cancellation. The device test exercises real app wiring.</p>',
    files=glob('test/**/*.dart')+glob('integration_test/*.dart')+['tool/contract_check.sh'],verify='fvm flutter test\nbash tool/contract_check.sh http://localhost:8080\nmake integration HOST=10.0.2.2',checkpoint='Local tests pass, then device integration tests run against the server.',trouble='Do not use pumpAndSettle as a substitute for waiting for an external page. Give network-driven assertions a bounded wait. Device failures need emulator logs, not just rerunning a unit test.')
chapter('Build Android and iOS', 'Create reproducible native artifacts with the required host settings.',
    '<p>Flutter generates the native host at project creation. Apply the complete host files below to reproduce the reviewed settings. Android uses Java/Kotlin/Gradle; iOS uses Xcode and CocoaPods here. Debug HTTP settings allow local mocks. A debug-signed artifact is not ready for store distribution. iOS simulator builds need no Apple signing account.</p><p>For local Android JDK compatibility use the Java version reported by flutter doctor and supported by the generated Gradle wrapper. The deployment target must satisfy the plugins. Do not blanket-disable TLS checks to fix a network error.</p>',
    files=[p for p in ['android/gradlew','android/gradlew.bat','android/settings.gradle.kts','android/build.gradle.kts','android/gradle.properties','android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties','android/app/build.gradle.kts','android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml','android/app/src/debug/AndroidManifest.xml','android/app/src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml','ios/Podfile','ios/Runner/Info.plist','tool/patch_platforms.sh','.github/workflows/ci.yml'] if (ROOT/p).exists()],
    verify='fvm flutter pub get\nfvm dart format lib test tool integration_test\nfvm flutter analyze --fatal-infos\nfvm flutter test\nfvm flutter build apk --debug\nfvm flutter build ios --simulator --debug',checkpoint='Build artifacts are produced, or a specific toolchain limitation is recorded. CI runs the same pinned SDK checks.',trouble='Android SDK license acceptance is your decision; run the doctor command interactively. On non-macOS skip iOS builds and use a Mac CI runner. Review the implementation report for this machine’s actual build outcomes.')
chapter('Review architecture, assumptions and job evidence', 'Know exactly what this proof of concept demonstrates.',
    '<p>The final tree separates <code>features</code> (screens/controllers), <code>domain</code> (business values), <code>data</code> (orchestration), <code>integrations</code> (provider adapters), <code>core</code> (shared infrastructure) and <code>webview</code> (hybrid boundary). This is sufficient for this app; adding architectural layers without a need would make learning and maintenance harder.</p>',
    '<div class="diagram">features → data → integrations → core<br>domain supplies shared hotel values<br>app/providers connects the graph<br>tool/mock_server supplies independent demo services</div>'+code('\n'.join(sorted(str(p.relative_to(ROOT)) for p in ROOT.glob('lib/**/*.dart'))),'Final lib/ structure'),
    files=['docs/15-API-AUDIT.md','docs/16-JOB-REQUIREMENTS.md','docs/17-IMPLEMENTATION-REPORT.md'],verify='Review the audit and demonstrate the script in the job-requirements table.',checkpoint='You can distinguish working code, tested mock assumptions and production work still needed.')
chapter('Reproducibility, glossary and final checklist', 'Finish with a source-complete, reviewable application.',
    '<p>The lockfile below records the tested package resolution. After the earlier package install, replace your lockfile with this reference and run pub get again. Additional checked-in documentation and host files are included below for exact reproduction.</p>',
    files=['pubspec.lock']+[p for p in ['ios/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj','ios/Runner/AppDelegate.swift','ios/Runner/SceneDelegate.swift','ios/Flutter/AppFrameworkInfo.plist','ios/Runner/Runner.entitlements','.env.example','README.md'] if (ROOT/p).exists()],
    verify='fvm flutter pub get\nfvm dart format --output=none --set-exit-if-changed lib test tool integration_test\nfvm flutter analyze --fatal-infos\nfvm flutter test',checkpoint='Keep the app and lockfile in version control, document your device checks, and review all known limitations before presenting the POC.')
assert not set(glob('lib/**/*.dart')), 'Missing app sources: '+str(glob('lib/**/*.dart'))
assert not set(glob('tool/mock_server/*.dart')), 'Missing mock sources'

style='''*{box-sizing:border-box}html{scroll-behavior:smooth}body{margin:0;background:#f8f5ef;color:#252a2c;font:17px/1.7 system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif}header{background:#153d40;color:#fff;padding:64px max(24px,calc((100vw - 1080px)/2))}header h1{font:clamp(38px,6vw,72px)/1.05 Georgia,serif;max-width:850px;margin:12px 0 24px}header p{max-width:760px;color:#d2e8e3}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#92713f;font-weight:750}header .eyebrow{color:#e8c998}main{max-width:1080px;margin:auto;padding:24px}nav{padding:24px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #d6ded9}nav ol{columns:2;column-gap:44px}nav li{break-inside:avoid;margin:0 0 9px}a{color:#146568}article{scroll-margin-top:18px;padding:48px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #c8d3ce}h2{font:38px/1.2 Georgia,serif;color:#163e40;max-width:850px}h3{font-size:21px;margin-top:30px}p,li{max-width:88ch}.objective{font-size:20px}aside,.tip,.checkpoint{background:#edf2ef;border-left:4px solid #417b70;padding:15px 20px;margin:20px 0}aside{background:#fff0d8;border-color:#b98530}.checkpoint{background:#e4efe9}.diagram{padding:28px;border:1px solid #9cb6aa;background:#fff;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;line-height:2}.lesson{margin:36px 0;padding-bottom:10px}figure{margin:24px 0;border:1px solid #cbd4cf;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;background:#fff}figcaption{padding:10px 16px;background:#e6ece8;font:13px/1.5 ui-monospace,monospace;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}button{border:1px solid #728e82;background:white;color:#153d40;padding:7px 14px;cursor:pointer;border-radius:4px}button:focus-visible,a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #b67924;outline-offset:3px}pre{margin:0;padding:20px;overflow:auto;max-height:640px;font:13px/1.65 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Consolas,monospace;tab-size:2}p code,li code{font-size:.86em;background:#e8ece6;padding:2px 4px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.kw{color:#6e3888}.str{color:#976017}.com{color:#637970}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd5ce;padding:12px}footer{padding:40px 24px;text-align:center;color:#526762}@media(max-width:650px){main{padding:16px}nav ol{columns:1}h2{font-size:30px}header{padding:44px 24px}pre{font-size:12px}figcaption{align-items:flex-start}}@media print{body{background:white;font-size:11pt}nav ol{columns:2}button{display:none}pre{max-height:none;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:8pt}article{break-before:page}header{background:white;color:black}header p{color:black}}'''
glossary={'Widget':'A description of one part of the screen.','State':'Values that can change and affect the screen.','BuildContext':'The location of a widget in the widget tree.','Mounted':'A widget/provider is still alive; check after asynchronous work before using it.','Future':'One result available later.','Stream':'A sequence of events over time.','Provider':'A Riverpod definition that supplies a service or state.','Notifier':'An object exposing state and actions that replace it.','Repository':'A boundary that combines business-facing data operations.','DTO':'A type matching a serialized request or response.','JSON':'Text encoding for objects, lists and simple values.','HTTP status':'A numeric result: 200 success, 400 bad input, 401 unauthenticated, 403 forbidden, 404 missing, 409 conflict, 422 invalid fields, 503 unavailable.','Idempotency':'Repeating an operation has the same effect as doing it once.','BFF':'Backend for frontend: the application server mediating vendor systems.','CRS / PMS':'Central reservation system / property management system; their APIs serve different purposes.','Rate plan':'Pricing rules and benefits associated with a room offer.','Quote':'A priced offer for particular dates and occupancy.','Authorization':'A payment hold/approval, distinct from capturing funds.','Void':'Cancellation of an authorization.','WebView':'A native embedded browser.','Bridge':'Validated communication between web content and Dart.','Origin':'URL scheme, host and port used to define a web trust boundary.','PKCE':'Proof Key for Code Exchange; binds an OAuth authorization flow to its initiator.','Fixture':'Controlled test data.','Regression':'A defect in behavior that previously worked.','CI':'Continuous integration: automatic checks of committed changes.'}
end='<section id="glossary"><h2>Glossary</h2><dl>'+''.join(f'<dt><strong>{html.escape(k)}</strong></dt><dd>{html.escape(v)}</dd>' for k,v in glossary.items())+'</dl></section><section id="checklist"><h2>Final learner checklist</h2><ul>'+''.join('<li>'+s+'</li>' for s in ['Use the pinned Flutter and Dart versions and commit the regenerated lockfile.','Start mocks without vendor credentials; finish search, room selection, cart and simulated payment.','Verify four-night promotional prices survive re-quote.','Demonstrate error, empty and retry states and rejection of invalid reservations.','Run unit, widget, mock lifecycle and device integration tests.','Build Android and iOS where the host supports them; record exact limitations.','Check large text, small screen, dark mode and screen-reader navigation.','Keep secrets and real payment/guest data out of code and logs.','Explain the separate public Property Hub contract and all demo gateway assumptions.','Describe the job-ad traceability and production work still required.'])+'</ul><p>Future work: implement contracted provider adapters, durable server-side checkout and reconciliation, real identity, licensed images, stronger end-to-end accessibility/performance coverage, release signing and store distribution. The optional AI illustration adapter needs a separately verified current model contract before live use.</p></section>'
end += '<section id="sources"><h2>Official references</h2><p>Checked 14 September 2026. The SynXis overview could not be fetched; the linked public specification was read successfully.</p><ul><li><a href="https://docs.flutter.dev/install/archive">Flutter SDK archive</a></li><li><a href="https://developer.synxis.com/pms/property_hub/reservation/reference-documentation">SynXis Property Hub reference</a> · <a href="https://developer.synxis.com/sites/default/files/public/apidoc_specs/sphReservation4.29.0.yaml">4.29.0 OpenAPI specification</a></li><li><a href="https://www.contentful.com/developers/docs/references/content-delivery-api/links/">Contentful entry and asset links</a></li><li><a href="https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/industries/loyalty/guide/get-started.html">Salesforce Loyalty integration guide</a></li><li><a href="https://docs.leonardo.ai/reference/creategeneration">Current Leonardo.Ai generation reference</a></li></ul></section>'
# Highlight on load while keeping raw code text and clipboard faithful to source.
script=r'''document.querySelectorAll('.copy').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',async()=>{const text=b.closest('figure').querySelector('code').textContent;try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);b.textContent='Copied'}catch{const r=document.createRange();r.selectNodeContents(b.closest('figure').querySelector('code'));const s=window.getSelection();s.removeAllRanges();s.addRange(r);b.textContent='Selected — copy manually'}}));
const esc=s=>s.replace(/&/g,'&amp;').replace(/</g,'&lt;').replace(/>/g,'&gt;');
document.querySelectorAll('pre code').forEach(el=>{const t=el.textContent;const re=/(\/\/[^\n]*|'(?:[^'\\]|\\.)*'|\b(?:class|final|const|return|void|import|async|await|if|else|switch|required|super|this|extends|implements|enum|sealed)\b)/g;let at=0,out='',m;while((m=re.exec(t))){out+=esc(t.slice(at,m.index));let cls=m[0].startsWith('//')?'com':m[0].startsWith("'")?'str':'kw';out+='<span class="'+cls+'">'+esc(m[0])+'</span>';at=re.lastIndex}el.innerHTML=out+esc(t.slice(at))});'''
page='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>LuxeStays Build Handbook</title><style>'+style+'</style></head><body><header><p class="eyebrow">Build-along course · reviewed 14 September 2026</p><h1>Build LuxeStays,<br>one working stage at a time.</h1><p>From your first Dart value to a mock-backed hotel booking app. Complete source files, checkpoints and honest provider boundaries. Flutter 3.47.4 · Dart 3.13.3.</p></header><main><nav id="contents" aria-label="Table of contents"><h2>Course map</h2><p>Work in a fresh practice directory. Each stage depends on the one before it. Code marked complete replaces the whole named file; temporary examples are explicitly identified. Source blocks are embedded here, so this document needs no internet to read or copy.</p><ol>'+''.join(f'<li><a href="#stage-{i}">{html.escape(t)}</a></li>' for i,(t,_) in enumerate(chapters,1))+'</ol><a href="#glossary">Glossary</a> · <a href="#checklist">Final checklist</a></nav>'+''.join(text for _,text in chapters)+end+'</main><footer>LuxeStays · Source-complete learning edition · Synthetic services and data</footer><script>'+script+'</script></body></html>'
OUT.write_text(page)
(ROOT / 'docs/LuxeStays-Build-Handbook.html').write_text(page)
print(f'Generated {OUT}: {len(chapters)} stages; {len(included)} embedded source files; {len(page):,} characters.')
